This chapter explains a few preliminary steps and basic camera operations.

<PIC:Manual10_8>
{{image description: Strap attachment diagram on a Canon camera. Numbered arrows show threading the strap through the strap mount and buckle, looping it through, and pulling it tight.}}

Pass the end of the strap through the camera's strap mount from the bottom. Then pass it through the strap's buckle as shown in the illustration. Pull the strap to take up any slack and make sure the strap will not loosen from the buckle. The eyepiece cover is also attached to the strap. (p.89)

<PIC:Manual10_9>
{{image description: Close-up of a Canon strap or strap buckle on a camera strap, with a callout line pointing to the buckle area.}}

- When you remove the battery from the camera, be sure to reattach the cover to protect against short circuit.

<PIC:Manual10_10>
{{image description: Battery charger illustration showing the battery compartment cover or protective cover being lifted open with an arrow.}}

Align the battery front edge with the mark on the battery charger. While pressing down the battery, slide it in the direction of the arrow. To detach the battery, follow the above procedure in reverse.

<PIC:Manual10_11>
{{image description: Battery pack placed into the charger, with an arrow and a double-headed mark showing alignment of the battery and charger contacts.}}

